  "route_at_most_seven_steps": [
    "1. Prove literal normalized-count cube law probability/finite and actual integral=sum/2^n. Internally establish equality to the balanced Bool finite product. Finite measurable singleton structure gives every displayed and slice function L1; no caller measurability/domain assumptions.",
    "2. Produce genuine signed two-point Ent(a²,b²)<= (a-b)²/2 for every real a,b. Positive squares use only the necessary Rothaus defect derivative/MVT cut; extend zero branches with (a²/2)log2<=a²/2 via log_le_sub_one_of_pos at2, and signed values via sqrt(a²)=abs a plus reverse triangle inequality.",
    "3. Prove finite last-Bool split using Fin.snocEquiv and actual cube sums, and the exact entropy chain identity Ent_{n+1}(h²)=E_n Ent2(hT,hF)+Ent_n(g²), g=sqrt((hT²+hF²)/2). g² equals the conditional mean including both-zero pairs. This is finite algebra with actual L1, no entropy theorem as premise.",
    "4. Prove RMS flip contraction for all real slice values: (g(x)-g(flip_j x))² <=((hT(x)-hT(flip_j x))²+(hF(x)-hF(flip_j x))²)/2. Represent g as L2 norm of the slice pair divided by sqrt2; use absolute reverse norm inequality, actual L2 square norm identity and sqrt2²=2. No smoothness or positivity of g needed.",
    "5. Induct on n directly on the final LSI. n0 law is one-point and entropy/empty Dirichlet sum0. At successor apply step2 to conditional last entropy, IH to g, and step4 to remaining flip squares. Fin.snoc commutes with non-last flips; last flip swaps the two slices, so its averaged squared difference is exactly the single slice square. The coefficient remains1/2 without dimension loss.",
    "6. Export one genuine alln Bernoulli producer with the3 internally derived L1 outputs and exact inequality. Do not additionally export scalar restatement wrappers or demand Han/desired LSI as a premise. Upstream Han plus signed two-point remains a valid sufficient alternative if a separate Han consumer warrants it.",
    "7. A later compact Gaussian consumer substitutes h(epsilon)=f(sum_j signValue(epsilon_j)/sqrt(n+1)) into n+1. Its pushforward and flip-law adapters give actual bernoulli_logSobolev_app; still-unported entropy limit and flip-energy limit4 then yield GaussianLSI.gaussian_logSobolev_CompSmo with coefficient2. Finite-Hilbert tensorization/noncompact cutoff and source KL/Fisher/T2/W2 remain separate."
  ],
  "local_API_boundary": "Pinned Mathlib count, finite L1, finite sum integrals, Fin.snoc/sum and reverseL2 norm primitives are available as actual static APIs. ASTIS Product update/map/Fubini leaves are real local reusable parents; current LogSobolev bookkeeping is not this analytic inequality. No local Bernoulli/signedtwoPoint/Han producer found in bounded queries, not an exhaustive absence theorem.",
